text:
You will be shown a series of Java code snippets, which you should rate based on your estimation of readability.
Readability is your judgement about how easy a block of code is to understand.
For each snippet you should respond by rating its readability on a scale of 1 to 5.
1 indicates very bad readability and 5 indicates very good readability. 
Alternatively, you can type 6 to skip if you do not want to answer for the current snippet.


